00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.643
&gt;&gt; Bret: FINALLY, IF YOU’RE

00:11:51.644 --> 00:11:54.025
TALKING TO SOMEBODY IN KENTUCKY,

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.655
YOU’RE UP FOR REELECTION AS WELL

00:11:55.656 --> 00:11:56.437
WELL.

00:11:56.472 --> 00:11:59.256
WHAT DO YOU TELL THEM THIS RACE

00:11:59.291 --> 00:12:00.451
IS ABOUT?

00:12:00.453 --> 00:12:02.813
&gt;&gt; WELL, IN THE KENTUCKY RACE,

00:12:02.814 --> 00:12:04.222
IT’S A LITTLE DIFFERENT FROM

00:12:04.224 --> 00:12:05.016
OTHERS.

00:12:05.017 --> 00:12:06.739
WHAT I TELL MY CONSTITUENCIES

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:07.792
I’M 1 OF 4 CONGRESSIONAL

00:12:07.827 --> 00:12:08.261
LEADERS.

00:12:08.262 --> 00:12:10.461
I AM THE ONLY ONE NOT FROM

00:12:10.463 --> 00:12:13.714
CALIFORNIA OR NEW YORK AND THAT

00:12:13.749 --> 00:12:15.300
I AM UNIQUELY SITUATED TO LOOK

00:12:15.301 --> 00:12:17.938
OUT FOR MIDDLE AMERICA AND IN

00:12:17.939 --> 00:12:18.858
